# Documentation First

The documentation is the source of truth.

## General Rules

- Never update code and documentation in the same task unless explicitly requested.
- Documentation must only describe completed or production-ready work.
- Never document features that are still under development.
- Preserve historical decisions and project history.
- Prefer updating existing documents over creating new ones.
- Keep document structure and writing style consistent.
- Maintain valid internal references.
- Do not rename documentation files unless explicitly instructed.

## STDP Rules

- Treat the production website as the authoritative reference.
- Reconcile documentation against the current repository before editing.
- Preserve documentation-first development principles.
- Keep updates factual rather than promotional.
- Mark assumptions clearly instead of presenting them as facts.

## Git Rules

- Never commit changes.
- Never push changes.
- Leave all edits uncommitted for review.